senses.gloss:
śaṅkha (also written saṃkha, Mv),
(1) m. (Pali saṅkha), n. of one of the four ‘great treasures’, (saṃkha) Mv 〔iii.383.18〕, and of the ‘king’ who presides over it, Divy 〔61.4〕 (see s.v. elapatra); as a nāga, known in Skt.; Divy 〔61.4〕 mentions this Ś. in juxtaposition with (2) but the relation between them is not made clear; in Pali the two have no connexion, (1) being only a ‘treasure’ DN comm. 〔i.284.8 f.〕;
(2) (= Pali id., DPPN Saṅkha 3), n. of a future emperor: Divy 〔60.14 ff.〕;
(3) n. of a rākṣasa, = Śaṅkhanābha: Divy 〔104.8〕.
